       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol, and I don't know of any standard indication for amlodipine 50 mg once daily. The dose is 5 times the labeled maximum, and an error could cause profound, prolonged hypotension and shock. I'm treating the protocol as a claim, not as something I can confirm, so I'm not comfortable entering it myself.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the usual range.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily now, and the team can titrate from there.\n- **Use the protocol pathway.** If a pharmacist-reviewed protocol exists, the order should be able to go through an order set or a documented override. That would link to the protocol and let pharmacy verify it. I can't do that from here.\n- **Re-check the dose with the pharmacist.** If they reviewed it, they can confirm the exact dose. A transcription error is also possible, for example 5 mg written as 50 mg.\n\nI can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily if you tell me which one you want."
